+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` tracks a losing *streak* rather than overall profit or a time window: if the last `trade_limit` trades for a pair all closed with a loss, back-to-back, that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`). A single winning trade resets the streak.
+
+By default, the same streak is also tracked across all pairs combined - if `trade_limit` losing trades happen in a row anywhere in the bot, all pairs are locked, not just the one that closed last. Set `only_per_pair` to true to disable this bot-wide check and only lock the individual pair.
+
+Since this protection does not consider `lookback_period`, it will keep re-triggering (and re-extending the lock) for as long as the pair (or the bot) keeps losing immediately after the lock expires.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair, and the bot as a whole, for 12 candles after 4 consecutive losing trades.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "only_per_pair": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
